# 1 is the seated value; the next 1 is its destructor on the assignment; 2 is the
# replacement; the last 2 is the epilogue tearing that one down. a store with no
# drop prints 1 / 2 / 2
--- OUT --->
1
1
2
2
--- RAST --->
# the drop hangs off the assignment, over the static itself. Tracked declares a
# destructor, so that is the call - $deinit is only synthesized when the teardown
# has to reach inside
CHECK: destroys old:
CHECK: call destructor(addrof<Tracked&>(static_property<Tracked>
